# UI design consistency

Use a single design reference for all UI work, for example `design/template.html` in this project. Read it before building any page or component.

## Colours
- Use only named colour tokens defined once in the theme (Tailwind config or CSS variables): background, surface, text, muted text, border, accent, success, warning, error.
- Do not write raw hex, rgb or hsl values in components.
- Use one accent colour per screen, for the main action and active states only.

## Type
- Use the project's font stack and type scale only. Do not add fonts.
- Body text is at least 15px with a line height of 1.6 or more.
- Use sentence case for headings and buttons.

## Spacing and layout
- Use the spacing scale (4px base). Avoid one-off margins and paddings.
- Give sections generous vertical padding and keep text columns under about 70 characters wide.
- Every page must work at 375px wide with no horizontal scroll. Check 375, 768 and 1440.

## Components
- Search the components folder before creating UI. Reuse existing buttons, inputs, cards, badges, modals and navigation.
- If a component needs a new look, add a variant to it. Do not create a second, slightly different copy.
- Every interactive element has hover, focus-visible, active and disabled states, and touch targets of at least 44px on phones.

## Content
- Use real copy, never lorem ipsum. Headlines state an outcome in a few words.
- Use one icon set at one stroke width. No emoji in the interface.
- Design empty, loading and error states instead of leaving them blank.

## Before finishing
- List the existing components you reused and any you created.
- Search your changes for raw colour values, new fonts and one-off spacing, and replace them with tokens.

Adapted from the BrowserMoon design rules for AI coding tools (browsermoon.com).
